Red Team Week 1 Infrastructure Build Report

Objective: I deployed a segmented, firewalled network architecture (Management, Red Team, Target) using VirtualBox, 
pfSense, Kali Linux, and Metasploitable 2 to meet the Week 1 requirements.

1. Prerequisites and Environment
I used my dual-booted Kali Linux machine as the host OS and installed VirtualBox as the hypervisor. 
I downloaded the required ISOs for pfSense CE v2.7.x and Metasploitable 2.

I ran these commands in my Kali terminal to download the necessary files:

cd ~/Downloads

I downloaded pfSense CE 2.7.2 by running:
wget -q --show-progress -O - https://atxfiles.netgate.com/mirror/downloads/pfSense-CE-2.7.2-RELEASE-amd64.iso.gz | gzip -d -c > pfSense-CE-2.7.2-RELEASE-amd64.iso

I downloaded and extracted Metasploitable 2 by running:
wget https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/metasploitable/Metasploitable2/Metasploitable2-Linux.zip
unzip Metasploitable2-Linux.zip

2. VirtualBox Network Infrastructure (Phase 1)
I configured the virtual network wires before starting any VMs.

A. Host-Only Networks
I discovered VirtualBox restricts Host-Only IPs by default, so I allowed custom ranges by running:
echo "* 10.0.0.0/8 192.168.0.0/16" | sudo tee /etc/vbox/networks.conf

I created the Management Network (vboxnet0) by running:
sudo VBoxManage hostonlyif create
sudo VBoxManage hostonlyif ipconfig vboxnet0 --ip 192.168.1.1 --netmask 255.255.255.0

I created the Red Team Network (vboxnet1) by running:
sudo VBoxManage hostonlyif create
sudo VBoxManage hostonlyif ipconfig vboxnet1 --ip 10.10.10.1 --netmask 255.255.255.0

B. VM Adapter Assignments
I opened the VirtualBox GUI and assigned the adapters as follows:

For the pfSense VM, I set:
Adapter 1 (WAN): Bridged Adapter (Host Wi-Fi)
Adapter 2 (LAN): Host-only Adapter (vboxnet0)
Adapter 3 (OPT1): Host-only Adapter (vboxnet1)
Adapter 4 (OPT2): Internal Network (Target_Net)

For the Metasploitable VM, I set:
Adapter 1: Internal Network (Target_Net)

3. Operating System Configurations (Phase 2)

A. pfSense Router Setup
I booted pfSense and assigned the interfaces at the console by selecting option 1:
I set WAN = em0, LAN = em1, OPT1 = em2, OPT2 = em3.

I set the IPs via Console Option 2:
For LAN (Management), I set 192.168.1.2/24 and disabled DHCP.
For OPT1 (Red Team), I set 10.10.10.2/24 and disabled DHCP.
For OPT2 (Target), I set 10.20.20.1/24 and disabled DHCP.

B. Metasploitable 2 Target Setup
I logged into Metasploitable using msfadmin/msfadmin.
I edited the network file by running: sudo nano /etc/network/interfaces
I configured it exactly as:
auto eth0
iface eth0 inet static
address 10.20.20.100
netmask 255.255.255.0
gateway 10.20.20.1
I applied the settings by running: sudo /etc/init.d/networking restart

4. Host Kali Routing (Phase 3)
Since Kali is my physical host, I manually attached it to the virtual networks by running these commands in the Kali terminal:

I assigned the Management IP by running:
sudo ip addr add 192.168.1.100/24 dev vboxnet0
sudo ip link set vboxnet0 up

I assigned the Red Team IP by running:
sudo ip addr del 10.10.10.1/24 dev vboxnet1 2>/dev/null
sudo ip addr add 10.10.10.50/24 dev vboxnet1
sudo ip link set vboxnet1 up

I added the route to the target network via pfSense by running:
sudo ip route add 10.20.20.0/24 via 10.10.10.2 dev vboxnet1

5. Firewall Authorization (Phase 4)
Traffic was initially blocked by pfSense's default deny policy.
I logged into the pfSense WebGUI from my Kali browser at https://192.168.1.2 using admin/pfsense.
I navigated to Firewall -> Rules -> OPT1 (Red Team).
I clicked Add and configured the rule:
Action: Pass
Protocol: Any
Source: any
Destination: any
I clicked Save, and then I clicked Apply Changes, which was the critical step to make the rule active.

6. Validation
From my Kali terminal, I tested the connectivity.

I tested the connection to the Gateway by running:
ping -c 3 10.10.10.2

I tested the connection to the Target by running:
ping -c 3 10.20.20.100

I verified the target ports were exposed by running:
nmap -sV 10.20.20.100

Result: The pings returned replies and Nmap showed open ports (FTP, SSH, HTTP, etc.). The Week 1 network infrastructure is 100% operational.

Maintenance Note
Because Kali is my host OS, I noted that the vboxnet IP assignments are not persistent across reboots. 
If my Kali machine restarts, I must re-run the commands in Phase 3 to restore connectivity.
